{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is SE-PE-01: grammar-guided node reduction on a parse tree. I need to implement `solve(case)` that:\n\n1. Takes a case with `nodes` and `required_symbols`\n2. Returns `removed_node_ids` and `retained_node_ids`\n\nKey rules:\n- Never remove root, a required symbol node, or a node with retained children\n- Consider deeper nodes before shallower nodes (process deep-first)\n- Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\n- Use node ID as stable tie-break at equal depth\n- Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order\n\nLet me think through the algorithm:\n\n1. Build the tree structure\n2. Process nodes in order: deeper nodes first, tie-break by node ID\n3. For each node (in that order), check if it's removable:\n   - Not removable if `removable=false`\n   - Not removable if its symbol is in `required_symbols`\n   - Not removable if it has children that are still retained\n   - Not removable if removing it would cause some required symbol to have no representation\n4. If removable, remove it (add to removed list)\n5. Return `removed_node_ids` (in order of removal) and `retained_node_ids` (sorted)\n\nWait, let me re-read: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nSo \"a required symbol\" means a node whose symbol is in required_symbols.\n\n\"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" - this means after removing the node, every symbol in required_symbols must still have at least one node in the retained set.\n\nThe order of processing: \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes\" and \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\"\n\nSo sort by (depth descending, node_id ascending) and process in that order.\n\nLet me think about the sorting of node IDs. The node IDs are strings like \"root\", \"n1\", \"n2\", etc. String comparison would give: \"n1\" \u003c \"n2\" \u003c \"n3\" etc. which seems right.\n\nActually wait - \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth\" - this means at the same depth, process in ascending node ID order.\n\nLet me trace through case 0:\n- Nodes:\n  - root: depth 0, removable=false, symbol=root\n  - n1: depth 1, removable=false, symbol=s1\n  - n2: depth 1, removable=true, symbol=s2\n  - n3: depth 1, removable=false, symbol=s0\n  - n4: depth 2, removable=true, symbol=s1\n  - n5: depth 2, removable=false, symbol=s2\n  - n6: depth 2, removable=true, symbol=s0\n\n- required_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nProcessing order (deeper first, then by node ID):\n- Depth 2: n4, n5, n6\n- Depth 1: n1, n2, n3\n- Depth 0: root\n\nProcessing n4 (depth 2, removable=true, symbol=s1):\n- Check: is symbol in required_symbols? s1 is required.\n- So cannot remove n4 if removing it leaves no s1 node.\n- Current retained nodes with symbol s1: n1 (s1), n4 (s1)\n- If we remove n4, n1 still has s1, so s1 is still represented.\n- n4 has no children (no node has parent n4), so no retained children concern.\n- Can we remove n4? Yes, all required symbols remain (root has root node, s1 has n1).\n- Remove n4.\n\nProcessing n5 (depth 2, removable=false):\n- removable=false, so skip.\n\nProcessing n6 (depth 2, removable=true, symbol=s0):\n- s0 not in required_symbols.\n- n6 has no children.\n- If remove n6, required symbols: root (root node retained), s1 (n1 retained). Both still present.\n- Remove n6.\n\nProcessing n1 (depth 1, removable=false):\n- removable=false, skip.\n\nProcessing n2 (depth 1, removable=true, symbol=s2):\n- s2 not in required_symbols.\n- Check children of n2: n4 was removed. No retained children.\n- If remove n2, required: root (retained), s1 (n1 retained). OK.\n- Remove n2.\n\nProcessing n3 (depth 1, removable=false):\n- removable=false, skip.\n\nProcessing root (depth 0, removable=false):\n- Skip.\n\nResult:\n- removed: [n4, n6, n2] (in order of removal)\n- retained: [root, n1, n3, n5] (sorted)\n\nHow to sort retained IDs? The problem says \"Return sorted retained IDs\". Sorted by what? Probably string sort or perhaps by some tree order. Let me re-read: \"Return sorted retained IDs\" - I'll assume lexicographic/alphabetical sort for simplicity, since no other order is specified.\n\nSorted: n1, n3, n5, root (alphabetical: n1 \u003c n3 \u003c n5 \u003c root)\n\nWait, comparing strings: \"n1\" \u003c \"n3\" \u003c \"n5\" \u003c \"root\" alphabetically. Yes.\n\nNow let me code this up:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Build data structures\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Track retained status\n    retained = {n[\"id\"]: True for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Get symbols represented by retained nodes\n    def get_retained_symbols():\n        return {node_map[nid][\"symbol\"] for nid, r in retained.items() if r}\n    \n    # Sort: deeper first, then by node ID ascending\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    removed_order = []\n    \n    for n in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = n[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Cannot remove if not removable\n        if not n[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Cannot remove if symbol is required (but need to check if removal keeps it represented)\n        # Actually: check if any retained children exist\n        has_retained_children = any(retained[c] for c in children[nid])\n        if has_retained_children:\n            continue\n        \n        # Tentatively remove: check if all required symbols remain\n        # Remove nid from retained temporarily\n        retained[nid] = False\n        retained_syms = get_retained_symbols()\n        \n        if required_symbols.issubset(retained_syms):\n            # OK to remove\n            removed_order.append(nid)\n        else:\n            # Cannot remove, restore\n            retained[nid] = True\n    \n    retained_ids = sorted(nid for nid, r in retained.items() if r)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_ids\n    }\n```\n\nWait, the rule says \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" The \"required symbol\" check - does this mean a node whose symbol is in required_symbols, OR does it mean we check whether required symbols remain represented? \n\nReading again: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children. Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\"\n\nSo:\n1. Never remove root (node with parent=null, or symbol=\"root\"?)\n2. Never remove a node whose symbol is a required symbol (hard constraint)\n3. Never remove a node with retained children (hard constraint)\n4. Only remove if all required symbols still represented after removal (additional check)\n\nHmm, but if rule 2 is \"never remove a node whose symbol is in required_symbols\", then we'd never remove n4 (s1 is required), but that seems overly restrictive. Let me reconsider.\n\nActually, rule 2 might mean \"never remove a node if doing so would eliminate the last occurrence of a required symbol\" - which is essentially what rule 4 says. So maybe rules 2 and 4 are saying the same thing differently.\n\nOr \"required symbol\" in rule 2 means the literal \"required_symbols\" concept - i.e., symbols that are required, meaning we can never remove them if they're the last representative. This is exactly what rule 4 says.\n\nBut if rule 2 means \"never remove any node whose symbol is in required_symbols\" (regardless of other occurrences), then n4 (symbol s1, which is required) can never be removed even if n1 also has s1.\n\nLet me look at the fixture cases to understand... All cases have required_symbols = [\"root\", \"s1\"]. The only nodes with s1 are n1 (not removable anyway) and n4 (removable). If rule 2 means we can't remove n4 because its symbol s1 is required, then n4 would always be retained.\n\nBut that seems odd. I think the more sensible interpretation is: \"never remove a node if it's the last representative of a required symbol\" - which is what rule 4 (tentative check) enforces.\n\nLet me re-read the candidate artifact more carefully: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nI think \"a required symbol\" here means \"a node whose symbol is listed in required_symbols\". Combined with rule 4, this means:\n- Hard constraint: never remove if symbol is required (regardless of other nodes)\n- OR it means: check that all required symbols remain represented (soft check)\n\nActually I think these might be two separate constraints that both apply:\n- Never remove a node if its symbol is in required_symbols (HARD - prevents removal even if other nodes have the same symbol)\n- Never remove a node if removing it would leave some required symbol with no representation\n\nIf the hard constraint applies, then n4 (symbol s1, required) can NEVER be removed, even though n1 also has s1.\n\nThis interpretation would change the results:\n\nCase 0:\n- n4: symbol=s1 (required) → cannot remove\n- n6: removable=true, symbol=s0, no children → can remove (s0 not required, all required still present)\n- n2: removable=true, symbol=s2, child n4 is retained → has retained children, cannot remove\n\nSo: removed=[n6], retained=[root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5]\n\nHmm, but that doesn't feel like a very good reduction algorithm either, since we'd rarely be able to remove anything useful.\n\nActually, maybe \"a required symbol\" in that sentence means something else - like the node is a required symbol node specifically (like a special terminal node), not just any node whose symbol happens to be in required_symbols.\n\nLet me re-read the task description: \"Reduce a registered parse tree through grammar-valid deletion and replacement candidates while preserving an interestingness oracle.\"\n\nThis is Perses-style reduction. In Perses, the goal is to reduce the tree while preserving some property (interestingness). The required_symbols list defines which symbol types must remain in the tree.\n\nI think the constraint \"never remove a required symbol\" means: don't remove a node if doing so would cause a required symbol type to disappear from the tree. This is exactly what \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" says.\n\nSo rules 2 and 4 are the same constraint, just stated differently. Rule 2 is the principle, rule 4 is how to implement it (tentatively remove, check, restore if needed).\n\nSo my original algorithm is correct. Let me also make sure about what \"retained children\" means - it means children in the current retained set (after previous removals).\n\nLet me also double-check: the rule says \"never remove root\" - root has removable=false anyway in all fixtures, so this is consistent.\n\nLet me also re-read: \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\" - I'm sorting by (-depth, node_id) where node_id is a string. This gives alphabetical order within same depth. n1 \u003c n2 \u003c n3 etc. which makes sense.\n\nI think my algorithm is correct. Let me verify with the fixture:\n\nCase 0 trace:\n- Processing order: n4 (depth 2), n5 (depth 2), n6 (depth 2), n1 (depth 1), n2 (depth 1), n3 (depth 1), root (depth 0)\n  - Actually alphabetical at depth 2: n4 \u003c n5 \u003c n6, correct.\n\nn4: removable=true, symbol=s1\n- Has retained children? No (n4 has no children)\n- Tentatively remove: retained becomes {root, n1, n2, n3, n5, n6}\n- Symbols: root (root), s1 (n1), s2 (n2, n5), s0 (n3, n6)\n- Required: root ✓, s1 ✓\n- Remove n4. removed=[n4]\n\nn5: removable=false → skip\n\nn6: removable=true, symbol=s0\n- Has retained children? No\n- Tentatively remove: retained becomes {root, n1, n2, n3, n5}\n- Symbols: root (root), s1 (n1), s2 (n2, n5), s0 (n3)\n- Required: root ✓, s1 ✓\n- Remove n6. removed=[n4, n6]\n\nn1: removable=false → skip\n\nn2: removable=true, symbol=s2\n- Has retained children? children of n2: [n4]. n4 is NOT retained (removed). So no retained children.\n- Tentatively remove: retained becomes {root, n1, n3, n5}\n- Symbols: root (root), s1 (n1), s2 (n5), s0 (n3)\n- Required: root ✓, s1 ✓\n- Remove n2. removed=[n4, n6, n2]\n\nn3: removable=false → skip\n\nroot: removable=false → skip\n\nFinal:\n- removed_node_ids: [\"n4\", \"n6\", \"n2\"]\n- retained_node_ids: [\"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\"] (sorted alphabetically)\n\nThis looks like a reasonable answer. The algorithm correctly reduces the tree.\n\nNow let me write the clean implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Build lookup and children index\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Track which nodes are currently retained\n    retained = {n[\"id\"]: True for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Process nodes: deeper first, tie-break by node ID (ascending)\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    removed_order = []\n    \n    for n in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = n[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Skip non-removable nodes\n        if not n[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip if has any retained children\n        if any(retained[c] for c in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        # Tentatively remove and check if all required symbols remain\n        retained[nid] = False\n        retained_symbols = {node_map[rid][\"symbol\"] for rid, r in retained.items() if r}\n        \n        if required_symbols.issubset(retained_symbols):\n            removed_order.append(nid)\n        else:\n            # Restore\n            retained[nid] = True\n    \n    retained_ids = sorted(nid for nid, r in retained.items() if r)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_ids\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Let me format it as the required JSON response.\n\nThe response must be exactly one JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    # Build lookup and children index\\n    node_map = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None:\\n            children[n[\\\"parent\\\"]].append(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    # Track which nodes are currently retained\\n    retained = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: True for n in nodes}\\n\\n    # Process nodes: deeper first, tie-break by node ID ascending (stable)\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    removed_order = []\\n\\n    for n in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = n[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Hard constraint: skip non-removable nodes\\n        if not n[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Hard constraint: skip if any retained children exist\\n        if any(retained[c] for c in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Tentatively remove and verify all required symbols remain represented\\n        retained[nid] = False\\n        retained_symbols = {node_map[rid][\\\"symbol\\\"] for rid, r in retained.items() if r}\\n\\n        if required_symbols.issubset(retained_symbols):\\n            # Removal is valid; commit it\\n            removed_order.append(nid)\\n        else:\\n            # Removing this node would drop a required symbol; restore\\n            retained[nid] = True\\n\\n    retained_ids = sorted(nid for nid, r in retained.items() if r)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removed_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": retained_ids\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01iIV0a2tknHpphgXwF1AhIF","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2412},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2412,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":50,"output_tokens":4409,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3938},"service_tier":"standard"}}